EXERCISE 10
Explore a dataset, identify trends and outliers, create basic visuals, and present insights
Objective
To explore a real-world dataset, identify trends and outliers, create meaningful visuals, and communicate insights effectively using Power BI.
Procedure
Step 1: Load the Dataset
Open Power BI Desktop.
Click Home → Get Data.
Select the dataset (Excel / CSV / Database).
Click Load.
Step 2: Clean and Model the Data
Data Cleaning (Power Query):
Click Transform Data.
Perform the following:
Remove duplicates
Handle missing values
Rename columns
Change data types
Click Close & Apply.
Data Modeling:
Open Model View.
Create proper relationships.
Verify cardinality and filter direction.
Step 3: Explore Data and Identify Patterns
Use Data View to inspect distributions.
Create quick visuals:
Sales by Year → Trend analysis
Sales by Category → Performance comparison
Identify:
Increasing / decreasing trends
Sseasonal patterns
High or low-performing categories


Step 4: Identify Outliers
Create:
Column charts
Line charts
Tables with sorting
Look for:
Extremely high or low values
Sudden spikes or drops
Use Top N filter or conditional formatting to highlight outliers.
Step 5: Create Dashboard
Combine:
KPI Cards
Charts
Tables
Slicers
Ensure all visuals interact properly.
Apply consistent formatting.
Step 6: Write Key Insights
Add insights using Text Boxes or prepare a separate report.
Example Insights:
Sales increased steadily over the last 3 years.
The Electronics category contributes the highest revenue.
Certain regions show unusually low sales indicating potential issues.
A few products generate exceptionally high profits.
Expected Output
Interactive dashboard showing trends and outliers
Clean and structured visuals
Clear insight summary based on data analysis



